title: Mantle cell lymphoma
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Hallmark:'' ''t(11;14)(q13;q32)'' juxtaposes ''CCND1'' with ''IGH'', driving ''cyclin D1 overexpression''.
* ''Presentation:'' Usually older men with advanced disease: lymphadenopathy, splenomegaly, marrow/blood involvement ± lymphocytosis, cytopenias, or B symptoms. Extranodal sites include the ''gastrointestinal tract'' and Waldeyer’s ring. Leukemic non-nodal disease may have little adenopathy and often lacks SOX11.
* ''GI pearl:'' ''Multiple lymphomatous polyposis'' is classic; microscopic involvement can occur without symptoms or visible polyps. Evaluate GI symptoms with endoscopy/biopsy. Upper/lower endoscopy is needed to confirm apparent stage I–II disease; routine screening in established advanced disease rarely changes management. Negative PET/CT does not exclude GI involvement.
* ''Diagnosis/immunophenotype:'' Obtain adequate tissue for histology, immunohistochemistry, and flow cytometry. Typical profile: ''CD19+, bright CD20+, CD5+, FMC7+, cyclin D1+, SOX11+; CD10−, CD23−''. Unlike chronic lymphocytic leukemia, CD20/surface immunoglobulin are usually bright. CD23+ or CD5− exceptions occur. Use FISH for t(11;14) when needed; rare cyclin D1-negative cases warrant expert review and CCND2/CCND3 rearrangement testing.
* ''Work-up:'' [[Work-up of mantle cell lymphoma]] — NCCN diagnostic, staging, and pretreatment assessment.

Sources: ASH SAP, 9th ed., ch. 45, p. 560; ASCO SEP 2026, ch. 20, MCL (PDF p. 1166); NCCN B-Cell Lymphomas v4.2026 (May 20), MANT-1; Discussion MS-84–86; [[EHA–EU MCL 2025|https://doi.org/10.1002/hem3.70233]].

